[agent] ## Summary
[agent] I built the full FTI pipeline for PM2.5 forecasting entirely on Databricks (serverless, since classic clusters are disabled in this workspace). The data was uploaded to a UC volume, and a serverless notebook job (`mlpab7bc766_airq_pipeline`) ran all ingestion, feature engineering, training, and inference platform-side.
[agent] **Deliverables (all in `workspace.mlpab7bc766`, verified via read-back):**
[agent] | Object | Type | Status |
[agent] |---|---|---|
[agent] | `airq0ecd46` | Feature group (PK `date`) | ✅ 979 rows — weather + lag/seasonal features + `pm25` |
[agent] | `airqtd0ecd46` | Training dataset | ✅ assembled, NA-dropped, time-sorted |
[agent] | `airqmodel0ecd46` | Registered regressor (UC, v1 READY) | ✅ HistGradientBoosting, metrics logged |
[agent] | `airqpred0ecd46` | Feature table (PK `date`, `pm25_pred`) | ✅ 90 rows, all forecast days |
[agent] **Metrics (logged to the MLflow run / model):**
[agent] - **holdout_rmse = 2.043 µg/m³** — below the 2.222 target (baseline train-mean RMSE ≈ 2.88)
[agent] - train_rmse = 0.84
[agent] The model was trained on all history after honest evaluation on a time-ordered 80/20 holdout, then applied to every forecast row. Predictions look sensible (≈1.9–10.6 µg/m³).
[agent] **Online low-latency lookup — platform capability missing in this workspace.**
[agent] The requirement to expose `airqpred0ecd46` for online lookup could not be completed:
[agent] - **Online Tables** (the classic offline→online publish path) are **deprecated** — the platform hard-rejects creation: *"Creating new online table is not allowed."*
[agent] - I provisioned the replacement — a **Lakebase instance** (`mlpab7bc766-airqdb`, AVAILABLE), a database catalog, and a **synced database table** (`…airqpred0ecd46_online`) keyed by `date`. The synced table's backing DLT pipeline failed repeatedly and ended `SYNCED_TABLE_OFFLINE_FAILED` with a deterministic workspace-config error: **`[UNITY_CATALOG_INITIALIZATION_FAILED] … Metastore storage root URL does not exist.`**
[agent] The offline Delta managed tables write fine (the metastore catalog has per-catalog storage), but the synced-table/online-store DLT pipeline requires a **metastore-level storage root** that is not configured in this workspace. With online tables deprecated and synced tables blocked on that missing storage root, **there is no working online-serving path available here** — the offline predictions feature table is complete and correct, but the online half of the online/offline distinction cannot be materialized through the interface as configured.
